# Scanner artifacts: the default --results directory of `security vuln prune`,
# `security baseline` and `preset scan-verdicts`. Downloading a workflow's
# artifacts here and committing them swept 43 files and 201k lines into a branch
# (#323), and gitleaks — which scans every ref — then failed the Security job of
# every CI run in the repository on CVE text that pattern-matches an API token.
scan-results/

# Internal notes
.cidx/ideas/

# Staging files: the local hand-off between a `prepare` step and the `create`
# that consumes it, never committed. The release notes are the exception and
# stay tracked — they are the record of what a release said.
#
# release-version was missing from this list, so the file the v3.0.0 release
# left behind was tracked, and `release create` refused the next release on its
# own leftover: "you have uncommitted changes" about the artefact it had just
# written itself.
.cidx/tag-version
.cidx/tag-message
.cidx/release-version

#AI
.serena
.claude